\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thou say'st: take up thy cross,
\par O man, and follow Me, 
\par The night is black, the feet are slack;
\par Yet we would follow Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. But, O dear Lord, we cry,
\par That we Thy face could see:
\par Thy blessed face one moment's space-
\par Then might we follow Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Dim tracts of time divide
\par Those golden days from me;
\par Thy voice comes strange o'er years of change;
\par How can we follow Thee?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Comes faint and far Thy voice
\par From vales of Galilee;
\par Thy vision fades in ancient shades;
\par How should we follow Thee?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O heavy cross-of faith
\par In what we cannot see:
\par As once of yore Thyself restore,
\par And help to follow Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. If not as once Thou camest
\par In true humanity,
\par Come yet as Guest within the breast
\par That burns to follow Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Within our heart of hearts
\par In nearest nearness be;
\par Set up Thy throne within Thine own;
\par Go, Lord- we follow Thee. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

